          "Build explicit messaging on housing affordability, education funding adequacy, and healthcare access stability — the three quality-of-life concerns most likely to activate the college-educated, professional, and younger-adult segments in an affluent suburban district at $82,420 median income.",
          "Maintain active constituent engagement focused on property tax fairness, school funding transparency, and rural broadband/infrastructure equity — the practical governance concerns of a homeowner-majority, mid-affluent constituency that evaluates on whether government delivers functional services.",
          "Monitor for credible Democratic infrastructure development in adjacent districts or statewide; if Democratic resources and messaging capability materialize in central Iowa, IA-HD-14's current 100% margin offers no protection — the incumbent will lack any recent experience defending against organized opposition."
