          "Engage the ~3.8% demographic gap thoughtfully—the small Native American population (Oto-Missouri and potentially Sac and Fox Nation citizens) has specific governance needs around tribal sovereignty recognition, water rights, and healthcare access that deserve active constituent attention rather than passive assumption of alignment with the majority white constituency.",
          "Develop a retention strategy for young adults: at $59,053 median income and 20.9% college attainment, IA-HD-17 is losing young people to urban labor markets. Workforce development initiatives, broadband expansion, and small-business incentives that create pathways to middle-class work without requiring out-migration are durable political investments that prevent future demographic hollowing.",
          "Treat the 100% result as a floor that requires active maintenance rather than a ceiling that guarantees future dominance—any incumbent who becomes complacent about constituent service, fails to address economic anxiety as it shifts, or loses touch with the material concerns of working-class rural households will create the opening a future challenger needs to compete in this district."
