          "Do not assume the 59% margin is a safe floor; it is the result of active alignment between the district's interests and current representation. Any incumbent who campaigns on partisan identity rather than constituent service, or who neglects to address emerging concerns about property tax burden, school performance, or healthcare access, will find the 41% opposition more competitive than the current margin suggests.",
          "Engage the college-educated professional base specifically on education quality and workforce development: the 30.1% college attainment rate reflects a constituency invested in educational outcomes, and continued investment in school quality and the pathway from K-12 into professional careers is both a governance obligation and a political necessity.",
          "Recognize that this district's homogeneity means there are no demographic sub-constituencies to target selectively; representation must be comprehensive and constituent-centered across the entire homeowner and professional base, because every issue is being evaluated by the same prosperous, educated, and discerning electorate that generated the 59% result."
