          "Build visible relationships with Hispanic and other minority communities: at 2.69% Hispanic and 1.09% Black, these communities are small but present, and candidates who have invested in authentic constituent service with these communities are both better positioned to serve them and better able to demonstrate to educated swing voters that they take representation seriously.",
          "Do not treat 72% as a durable floor: a strong result in an affluent, educated suburban district can erode quickly if demographic change, a compelling challenger focused on persuasion rather than turnout, or genuine policy failure shifts educated swing voters' evaluation; active constituent engagement and a record of delivering on the material concerns of families in the district is the best insurance against a credible challenge."
