          "Build credibility through local economic development and cost-of-living solutions: a representative who can point to specific legislative wins on property tax relief, rural broadband infrastructure, or healthcare access is more durable in this constituency than one whose record emphasizes ideological positioning over material constituent outcomes.",
          "Avoid the assumption that 65% represents a stable floor: in a working-class district where most households live paycheck to paycheck, economic messaging from a credible challenger who speaks directly to cost-of-living concerns can shift 5-7 percentage points of the current coalition, making this seat materially less safe than the current margin suggests."
