          "Engage the renter cohort and younger household-formation voters directly: the 28.9% renter rate and 31.9 median age mean nearly 30% of the district is in active housing-cost transition — mortgage access, property tax fairness, and housing affordability are the material concerns that determine whether this group votes on economics or identity.",
