          { name: "Framing Governance as National Partisan Conflict Rather Than Local Problem-Solving", tag: "avoid", why: "IA-HD-45 is a state legislative district, not a congressional seat — and voters in a $126,276-income, 43.6% college-educated community evaluate their state representative primarily on local governance competence, not on national partisan positioning. A representative who campaigns on national Republican talking points rather than demonstrating specific knowledge of HD-45's local economic development priorities, infrastructure needs, and school governance challenges is ceding an opening to a Democratic challenger who can articulate a more compelling local vision. This constituency is less ideological and more pragmatic than partisan frameworks assume." }
