          "Lead with fiscal conservatism and property tax fairness: at $126,276 median income with 92% homeownership, this constituency evaluates on whether government is delivering efficient services, protecting property values, and managing tax burden — not on social issues or partisan tribal identity.",
          "Protect the 35% Democratic base from credible challenger recruitment by demonstrating superior constituent service, local economic development competence, and protection of neighborhood quality of life — the absence of a visible Democratic alternative is more important to holding this seat than the current 65% margin.",
          "Address school funding and governance explicitly: the combination of high income, high college education, and 38.8-year median age signals substantial concern with K-12 school quality, which is the primary driver of property values and family quality of life in affluent suburban districts like HD-45."
