          "Lead with university-town economic development and affordability: the 60.8% renter rate and 21.7-year median age identify a constituency under housing cost pressure; concrete policy on rental affordability, first-time homebuyer support, and the university-to-workforce transition is more electorally durable than abstract progressive positioning.",
          "Build constituent engagement infrastructure specifically designed for a young, educated, transient population: a renter-majority, university-town district has natural turnover; active civic participation programming, neighborhood association support, and transparent local decision-making processes convert the 100% baseline into genuinely earned and repeated support rather than taking the partisan default for granted.",
          "Avoid treating this as a settled seat: the 57.6% college attainment and high civic engagement expectations mean this constituency is capable of primary challenge or third-party organizing if local governance performance is perceived as inadequate; treat 100% as a mandate for exceptional performance on local issues, not a license for neglect."
