          { name: "Assuming Educational Attainment Automatically Translates to Party Loyalty", tag: "avoid", why: "While college-educated voters do trend Democratic, the 66.3% college-educated rate in IA-HD-50 means this constituency evaluates carefully on policy competence and responsiveness to their material concerns. Educated voters are more likely to defect if they perceive ineffective governance or inattention to issues affecting them—housing, childcare, student debt. The 100% margin depends on demonstrating concrete legislative achievement on issues this educated constituency cares about, not assuming their loyalty is automatic." }
