          "Invest heavily in vocational and skills-based education messaging—apprenticeships, technical credentials, union pathways—not college. With 78% of adults without a four-year degree, this framing is both authentic and persuasive.",
          "Avoid identity-politics framing entirely: no culture-war rhetoric, no demographic anxiety narratives, no urban-vs-rural populism. This district sees itself as self-reliant and economically integrated, not marginalized or under siege.",
          "Build local credibility through specific, named commitments to employers, schools, and civic institutions in the district. Abstract statewide ideology will lose to a candidate who names the manufacturing plant that needs support or the school that needs funding."
