          "Engage younger adults and renters as a distinct persuadion target: at 35.5% renter rate and 36.1 median age, nearly one-third of the district does not have property-ownership stakes and evaluates on housing affordability, student debt relief, and wage trajectory — a coalition that the incumbent has assembled but that is not guaranteed to remain stable if a credible alternative emerges.",
          "Avoid treating 56% as an ideological mandate: the 44% opposition in a majority-white, homeowner-heavy, middle-income district is a reminder that the current margin reflects performance evaluation by swing voters, not demographic destiny — any candidate who treats this as a safe seat and campaigns primarily to the base is making a strategic error.",
          "Maintain focus on material governance and local issues: in a demographically homogeneous district where identity-specific messaging carries less weight, school quality, property tax management, infrastructure, and local service delivery are the currency of persuasion that actually moves votes in IA-HD-71."
