          "Lead with older homeowner economic security: at 42.8 median age, $86,250 income, and 85% homeownership, this is a constituency with material assets and rising fixed costs. Medicare sustainability, property tax fairness, and rural healthcare access are the issues most likely to activate dissatisfaction if the incumbent is not addressing them with specificity.",
          "Engage the college-educated, higher-income segment on education quality and workforce development — the 27.3% college-attainment rate suggests a constituency with stakes in both secondary education and the pipeline to professional employment. Community investment in K-12 and post-secondary education is a material governance concern for families in this income and education bracket.",
          "Recognize that unopposed status is not a mandate to govern inattentively — it is an invitation to enter the district with a credible alternative if the incumbent has become disconnected from constituent concerns. Test the actual depth of the 100% by asking older homeowners what they wish their representative was doing differently."
