          "Defend the older white homeowner constituency on property tax burden and rural service delivery: the 72.3% homeowner rate at $64,615 income creates vulnerability to Republican messaging on tax fairness and rural hospital viability — specific legislative accomplishments on property tax assessment reform and rural infrastructure funding are necessary to hold this base.",
          "Recognize that 59-41 is a solid Democratic margin in Iowa but not a safe seat: the combination of Republican statewide momentum, rural economic distress, and concentrated Latino population creates a constituency that will evaluate based on whether the incumbent is delivering material improvements in their economic circumstances — inherited partisan loyalty is not the baseline assumption.",
          "Build visible presence in Latino community institutions and on worker safety issues: meat processing plant conditions, agricultural labor standards, and contractor safety in construction are the lived economic concerns of the 16.25% Hispanic/Latino constituency and are the most credible vulnerability for a Republican challenger to exploit if the Democratic incumbent is not actively engaged on these specific issues."
