          "Engage college-educated voters on education investment and workforce development: the 25.7% college-attainment rate and professional-class household profile depend on schools and higher education that produce competitive outcomes; frame education funding as an investment in residential value and economic opportunity, not as an ideological priority.",
          "Address aging constituent healthcare and retirement security: the 40.5 median age signals voters increasingly focused on Medicare sustainability, long-term care planning, and rural healthcare access; demonstrate concrete legislative attention to these concerns rather than assuming partisan alignment substitutes for constituent service.",
          "Monitor demographic drift and do not assume the 100% result represents durable consolidation: sustained attention to constituent concerns, accessibility, and responsiveness is essential to prevent drift toward Democratic or independent alternatives if voters conclude the incumbent is taking the district for granted."
