          { name: "Urban-Focused Progressive Policies", tag: "avoid", why: "With a small Asian population (1.01%), Black population (2.09%), and a low college-education rate (19.3%), this district has weak overlap with constituencies prioritizing urban renewal, diversity initiatives, or educational expansion rhetoric. Messaging centered on these themes will face structural headwinds and should be reframed around rural benefits—infrastructure in small towns, workforce development in existing industries—rather than urban-centric language." }
