          { name: "Neglecting Non-White Communities in a Majority-White District", tag: "avoid", why: "The 22%+ non-white population (Black 9.24%, Hispanic 7.41%, Asian 6.25%) is significant and diverse in its economic and social concerns, but can become invisible in a district where the dominant story is white college-educated renters. Economic mobility, workforce development, and healthcare access concerns specific to these communities require direct constituent engagement rather than assumption that demographic alignment guarantees automatic support; neglecting these communities creates space for alternative messaging on economic opportunity." }
