          { name: "Defaulting to Partisan Messaging Over Constituency Problem-Solving", tag: "avoid", why: "IA-SD-22's affluent, educated constituency evaluates candidates on concrete problem-solving — school quality, tax efficiency, healthcare access — rather than partisan rallying. A candidate whose messaging defaults to abstract ideological positioning (left or right) rather than specific, locally rooted answers to this community's actual governance challenges will find that the 48% opposition becomes recruitable. In a district where voters are economically secure enough to care about institutional competence and policy quality, whoever offers the more coherent, specific vision for serving this constituency's real needs will win the margin, regardless of the partisan label." }
