          "Do not treat 59-41 as a stable majority: the 41% opposition in a district this demographically aligned to Republican strength is a warning signal that affluent suburban voters are genuinely open to Democratic alternatives if they perceive the incumbent as underperforming on fiscal management, education, or quality-of-life delivery."
