          { name: "Ignoring Healthcare Cost Pressure on Middle-to-Upper-Middle-Class Households", tag: "avoid", why: "While $80,277 median household income is comfortable, healthcare costs and healthcare access are material concerns for suburban professionals — particularly as a family's income means both private insurance obligations and significant out-of-pocket exposure. An incumbent who does not credibly address healthcare cost management or healthcare access as a constituent priority will find that vulnerability exploited by an opponent who takes these cost pressures seriously and offers specific policy remedies to control them." }
