          { name: "Dismissing Minority Communities as Electorally Immaterial", tag: "avoid", why: "At 92.57% white, IA-SD-29 appears demographically homogeneous, but the remaining 7.43% of the population—2.67% Hispanic, 1.05% Asian, 0.86% Black, and likely ~2.85% multiracial or Native American—represents real households with real constituent needs around healthcare access, workplace discrimination, and economic opportunity. In a district this white-dominant, minority communities can become invisible in political communication and constituent service. Any candidate who provides active constituent engagement to Hispanic agricultural workers, Asian small-business owners, and Black residents demonstrates that representation is not contingent on population share—and builds goodwill that can matter in close races." }
