          "Avoid assuming the 66% is a stable floor: a district with this demographic profile should produce 70%+ Republican results in a state as deeply red as Iowa; the gap between that expectation and the actual 66% indicates real constituent dissatisfaction that will compound if left unaddressed through the next election cycle.",
          "Develop a credible narrative about what state government has delivered specifically for IA-SD-33 households on property taxes, healthcare access, and school funding; in a low-college-attainment district, constituents evaluate on concrete outcomes, not partisan messaging or abstract conservative positioning."
