          "Lead with working-class economic security: housing affordability for the 38.3% of renters, wage floor policy for the $60,327 median income constituency, and healthcare access that does not depend on college education or professional employment — these material concerns are where elections are won or lost in this district.",
          "Build specific, ongoing relationships with the Black, Hispanic, and American Indian communities; understand their distinct governance needs around criminal justice, economic opportunity, healthcare access, and tribal partnership — and translate that understanding into measurable legislative responsiveness that demonstrates you are actively serving them, not assuming their support.",
          "Prepare your organizational and messaging strategy for genuine competition; treat the next cycle as if the margin will be contested, and build a volunteer and donor network grounded in community relationships rather than assumed partisan dominance — the 100% result is your warning signal to deepen constituent work, not permission to coast."
